Subject: Make element-library preview handle drop without native HTML5 drop

Full-size element-library previews expose a large "drag onto the page" handle,
but that handle sits inside the preview overlay. Browser-native HTML5 drag/drop
can start from there while the VE overlay collapses, but some browsers never
deliver a usable drop event or omit the custom text/ve-drag payload by the time
the pointer reaches the page drop zone. The visible drop zones then do nothing.

Keep the existing native drag path for cards, rows and fallback behaviour, but
make the preview handle itself pointer-driven: while the pointer is down, the
library keeps the active drag payload, tracks visible <ve-drop-zone> targets
through open shadow roots, shows a Lit-rendered drag ghost, and calls the drop
zone directly on pointerup. Drop zones also accept the in-memory drag payload
as a fallback when dataTransfer is missing.

